{"reference":"Isaiah 38","book":"Isaiah","chapter":38,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Book of Isaiah","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Isaiah 38 belongs to a book that includes prophetic speech, first-person material, third-person narration, sign actions, and royal narratives. The book presents Isaiah son of Amoz as its named prophet, yet scholars also study its received form as the result of a long process of collection and editorial development; no detailed reconstruction has gained consensus. This makes it important to attend closely to the form of each passage and establish its speakers from the passage itself.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_038_266bfc1833c2cabc5e3a8237"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}